            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0840" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.119/315a suppl.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-14T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>116. Supplementing Department’s No. 91 April 23rd noon to which reply is awaited.
                    The Department is further informed that <pb facs="0841" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/>
                    in addition to Belgian consignment of arms delivered at Tientsin there have been
                    delivered to a Chinese arsenal from Great Britain steel materials for the
                    manufacture of munitions. Report by telegraph whether you consider that
                    complaints of violation of embargo by Belgian, British, Italian, and Japanese
                    interests are well founded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
